.vscode/
.idea/
# Live-integration OAuth tokens, at any depth. Anchored patterns (anything
# containing a slash) resolve relative to this file, so a path-specific
# pattern would cover only one suite; **/ covers every adapter's live-test
# folder.
**/.tokens.json
.playwright-mcp/
# Swagger/docs-server screenshots dropped at repo root during dev verification
/swagger-*.png
/invoice-*.png
/accounting-*.png
/crm-*.png
/landing-*.png
/combined-*.png

# Agent working directory (SDD plans, ratchet reports, session scratch). Same
# class as docs/superpowers/ below: OpenSteward's own development process, not
# anything an operator running this stack needs. Only `.superpowers/sdd/` is
# self-ignored by the tool that writes it, so a sibling folder would otherwise
# be swept in by `git add -A`.
.superpowers/

# Internal planning and research notes. These are working documents for
# OpenSteward's own development, not operator documentation, and docs-server
# serves everything under docs/ unauthenticated — it also bakes each file's
# body text into the search index shipped inside the published image. Keeping
# them out of the repo entirely is what stops them reaching self-hosters.
# scripts/build-search-index.ts also skips these paths, so a local working
# copy here still never ships.
docs/superpowers/
docs/research/

# Platform logos, fetched from the Brandfetch CDN rather than committed.
#
# Brandfetch's Logo API terms prohibit committing these files:
# "programmatic access to logo images is not permitted" and caching requires
# a written agreement with them. The files are also 1,474 other companies'
# trademarks, and the published docs-server image ships docs/ (the Dockerfile
# stages it into that image only), so committing them would redistribute
# those marks through GHCR and the AWS, Azure and GCP marketplace mirrors.
# .dockerignore keeps this directory out of every build context as well.
#
# Operators choose how they want logos via LOGO_SOURCE — see
# docs/operations/platform-logos.md. `none` (the default) needs nothing here;
# `local` populates this directory with `pnpm --filter integration-server
# fetch:logos`. Either way the bytes never enter git.
docs/platforms/logos/

# Vendored browser assets (Phosphor, htmx, Swagger UI, lunr), copied out of
# node_modules by packages/design-system/scripts/sync-vendor.ts on every build.
# These are served from /design/vendor/ so a self-hosted deployment makes no
# runtime request to unpkg or jsdelivr — see THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md. Generated,
# so not tracked; versions are pinned in design-system's package.json where
# Dependabot can see them.
packages/design-system/vendor/

# Operator license files (docs/deployment/license.md). docker-compose.yml
# mounts ./opensteward-license into integration-server; a customer's license
# never belongs in git. Anchored to the repo root: an unanchored `license.key`
# would also ignore a future test fixture of that name. A run from source
# resolves a relative OPENSTEWARD_LICENSE_FILE from apps/integration-server, so
# the same two names there; its default, data/license.key, is under data/.
/opensteward-license/
/license.key
/apps/integration-server/opensteward-license/
/apps/integration-server/license.key
